1
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:36,200
[This drama is fictional
and bears no resemblance to reality]

2
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,150
[Some scenes feature AI technology]

3
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:38,440
[All child and animal scenes
followed strict safety guidelines]

4
00:00:41,896 --> 00:00:46,460
Everyone will be waiting for your cue.

5
00:00:50,512 --> 00:00:52,084
Go ahead.

6
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:04,443
Ready...

7
00:01:07,647 --> 00:01:09,491
Action!

8
00:01:11,611 --> 00:01:13,409
[Episode 8]
Buy a paper!

9
00:01:13,409 --> 00:01:15,102
Take one!

10
00:01:15,102 --> 00:01:17,213
Hello.

11
00:01:17,213 --> 00:01:19,104
What do you think?

12
00:01:19,104 --> 00:01:23,367
Not under Wolhajeong's lights,
but here under the moonlight.

13
00:01:23,367 --> 00:01:24,671
I'm not sure.

14
00:01:24,671 --> 00:01:28,841
From every angle, you seem free of all worries.

15
00:01:30,486 --> 00:01:32,675
Let me see.

16
00:01:34,274 --> 00:01:37,470
From every angle...

17
00:01:37,470 --> 00:01:39,567
Truly beautiful.

18
00:01:41,831 --> 00:01:45,715
I mean myself, reflected in your eyes.

19
00:01:48,164 --> 00:01:51,590
How are you always joking?

20
00:01:59,468 --> 00:02:01,216
<i>It suits you well.</i>

21
00:02:14,247 --> 00:02:16,290
Oh Ha Na!

22
00:02:18,569 --> 00:02:20,915
Everyone, stop filming!

23
00:02:23,130 --> 00:02:24,686
What's with her?

24
00:02:25,313 --> 00:02:28,656
- Come with me.
- Mom, stop! It hurts!

25
00:02:28,656 --> 00:02:30,048
Oh my!

26
00:02:30,734 --> 00:02:33,000
What do you think you're doing?

27
00:02:33,687 --> 00:02:34,277
Cut.

28
00:02:34,277 --> 00:02:38,377
You just stamped that contract. How dare you...

29
00:02:38,377 --> 00:02:41,221
Enough. People are watching.

30
00:02:41,861 --> 00:02:44,880
A scandal won't help you.

31
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:49,980
As a mom shutting down a shoot,
or a CEO who lost her renewal.

32
00:03:04,190 --> 00:03:06,669
Surprise!

33
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:09,717
Pretty good acting, right?

34
00:03:12,763 --> 00:03:16,380
I didn't expect Yu Geon
and the director to step in.

35
00:03:17,054 --> 00:03:18,581
Right, Ha Na?

36
00:03:18,581 --> 00:03:20,415
Hey, smile.

37
00:03:21,303 --> 00:03:22,720
Everyone!

38
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:26,641
This was a surprise event Ha Na and I prepared.

39
00:03:26,641 --> 00:03:30,594
This is Ha Na's first starring film.

40
00:03:30,594 --> 00:03:32,694
We couldn't just let it pass.

41
00:03:32,694 --> 00:03:34,673
Sorry if we scared you.

42
00:03:34,673 --> 00:03:36,355
Sorry!

43
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:42,924
It was all an act to give you padded jackets.

44
00:03:42,924 --> 00:03:47,788
It'll get cold soon, so stay warm on set.

45
00:03:47,788 --> 00:03:50,506
Director Kang will hand them out.

46
00:03:50,506 --> 00:03:53,275
Please take good care of Ha Na.

47
00:03:53,275 --> 00:03:55,235
There he comes.

48
00:03:56,751 --> 00:03:58,682
Let's take a short break.

49
00:03:58,682 --> 00:04:00,657
Hello. The jackets are here!

50
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:02,284
They're free!

51
00:04:02,284 --> 00:04:04,111
An Su Hui!

52
00:04:04,111 --> 00:04:05,738
- Oh Ha Na!
- Oh Ha Na!

53
00:04:05,738 --> 00:04:07,142
- An Su Hui!
- An Su Hui!

54
00:04:07,142 --> 00:04:08,828
- Oh Ha Na!
- Oh Ha Na!

55
00:04:08,828 --> 00:04:10,905
- Stay warm.
- An Su Hui!

56
00:04:10,905 --> 00:04:12,544
- Oh Ha Na!
- Oh Ha Na!

57
00:04:12,544 --> 00:04:14,558
- An Su Hui!
- An Su Hui!

58
00:04:15,305 --> 00:04:17,382
Here you go!

59
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:19,379
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

60
00:04:19,379 --> 00:04:21,079
My pleasure.

61
00:04:22,556 --> 00:04:25,631
- We need to talk.
- That's what I wanted.

62
00:04:26,670 --> 00:04:27,888
Yeah.

63
00:04:27,888 --> 00:04:29,782
Stay warm.

64
00:04:29,782 --> 00:04:31,601
Stay warm!

65
00:04:36,269 --> 00:04:39,154
I'm warm-toned. Black isn't my color.

66
00:04:39,154 --> 00:04:42,192
"Warm-toned?" More like one-tenth-ton.

67
00:04:43,536 --> 00:04:46,733
I really thought we were shutting down.

68
00:04:46,733 --> 00:04:49,697
What kind of surprise is that terrifying?

69
00:04:49,697 --> 00:04:51,829
Maybe we really will shut down.

70
00:04:51,829 --> 00:04:53,065
What?

71
00:04:53,725 --> 00:04:57,621
The real act was pretending it was an act.

72
00:04:58,381 --> 00:05:01,592
Seok Gi heard everything.

73
00:05:01,592 --> 00:05:04,179
<i>Enough. People are watching.</i>

74
00:05:04,179 --> 00:05:06,227
<i>A scandal won't help you.</i>

75
00:05:06,227 --> 00:05:10,391
<i>As a mom shutting down a shoot,
or a CEO who lost her renewal.</i>

76
00:05:10,391 --> 00:05:12,321
<i>Surprise!</i>

77
00:05:12,321 --> 00:05:14,021
<i>Pretty good acting, right?</i>

78
00:05:14,021 --> 00:05:15,232
No way.

79
00:05:15,232 --> 00:05:17,058
I knew something was off.

80
00:05:17,058 --> 00:05:21,058
A star like Oh Ha Na joins,
and not one article?

81
00:05:21,058 --> 00:05:23,122
She just went on hiatus.

82
00:05:23,122 --> 00:05:26,409
Burnout? Please.

83
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:32,391
So the whole "surprise event" thing was a lie?

84
00:05:32,391 --> 00:05:36,015
And I was worshipping them like an idiot.

85
00:05:36,015 --> 00:05:39,494
What if their fight blows up on all of us?

86
00:05:39,494 --> 00:05:42,024
What if the whole project falls apart...

87
00:05:42,024 --> 00:05:43,969
Enough with the nonsense.

88
00:05:43,969 --> 00:05:46,622
Stop stirring things up.

89
00:05:46,622 --> 00:05:49,775
It hasn't even happened. Cut it out.

90
00:05:49,775 --> 00:05:51,839
Just keep the crew quiet.

91
00:05:51,839 --> 00:05:53,408
Got it.

92
00:05:54,262 --> 00:05:57,733
Badmouthing the set outside
only makes us look bad.

93
00:05:57,733 --> 00:06:00,594
- Yeah.
- Let's just do our jobs. Come on.

94
00:06:00,594 --> 00:06:01,778
- Yes.
- Let's go.

95
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:03,491
Wait.

96
00:06:04,693 --> 00:06:07,797
Cute little stunt you're pulling here.

97
00:06:07,797 --> 00:06:12,177
You thought once filming started, I'd be stuck?

98
00:06:12,177 --> 00:06:14,124
Do you know who I am?

99
00:06:14,124 --> 00:06:15,626
Shut this shoot down now!

100
00:06:15,626 --> 00:06:17,811
Everything stops until I say so.

101
00:06:17,811 --> 00:06:19,108
Mom.

102
00:06:19,108 --> 00:06:23,691
CEO An, you don't have that authority.

103
00:06:23,691 --> 00:06:25,862
No, I don't.

104
00:06:25,862 --> 00:06:29,178
But I do have power.

105
00:06:30,078 --> 00:06:32,615
I won't accept Oh Ha Na.

106
00:06:32,615 --> 00:06:34,882
Until she's out, I'm boycotting this.

107
00:06:34,882 --> 00:06:36,675
Get in, Yu Geon.

108
00:06:38,513 --> 00:06:40,143
Get in!

109
00:06:40,143 --> 00:06:42,469
You're not filming this.

110
00:06:42,469 --> 00:06:44,393
Fine.

111
00:06:44,393 --> 00:06:46,259
Then I'll...

112
00:06:46,936 --> 00:06:49,789
I'll withdraw from the project, CEO An.

113
00:06:49,789 --> 00:06:51,212
- Sim Yu Geon.
- Yu Geon.

114
00:06:51,212 --> 00:06:52,279
What?

115
00:06:52,279 --> 00:06:53,829
You know what that means?

116
00:06:53,829 --> 00:06:58,226
You'll never set foot in this industry again.

117
00:06:58,226 --> 00:07:00,084
I don't care.

118
00:07:00,084 --> 00:07:04,539
It was never my place anyway.

119
00:07:08,533 --> 00:07:10,302
Sorry, Yi Jae.

120
00:07:11,067 --> 00:07:13,065
I'm sorry, Soo Bin.

121
00:07:21,450 --> 00:07:23,347
Let's do that, then.

122
00:07:23,347 --> 00:07:26,384
Directors, find another male lead.

123
00:07:26,384 --> 00:07:30,031
With Ha Na's rumors, that won't be easy.

124
00:07:30,031 --> 00:07:31,737
Ma'am!

125
00:07:33,498 --> 00:07:36,201
The jackets are all handed out.

126
00:07:36,201 --> 00:07:38,920
I also left the directors' jackets...

127
00:07:40,167 --> 00:07:42,271
- Let's go.
- Yes, ma'am.

128
00:07:42,271 --> 00:07:43,971
Hurry.

129
00:07:44,639 --> 00:07:46,443
Yu Geon.

130
00:08:00,637 --> 00:08:02,674
Ha Na.

131
00:08:02,674 --> 00:08:07,294
I told you I think ahead,
even about what I can do next.

132
00:08:07,294 --> 00:08:09,318
Watch and learn.

133
00:08:09,318 --> 00:08:14,183
It all happened because of
that stupid rebellious attitude of yours.

134
00:08:29,483 --> 00:08:32,730
Let's call off today's shoot.

135
00:08:40,325 --> 00:08:41,332
Sorry.

136
00:08:41,332 --> 00:08:43,216
This is all because of me...

137
00:08:46,249 --> 00:08:48,673
It's not your fault.

138
00:08:48,673 --> 00:08:50,525
It's okay.

139
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,350
Hello.

140
00:09:08,350 --> 00:09:12,632
I'm Nam Ye Seo,
your new producer starting today.

141
00:09:12,632 --> 00:09:15,640
Hello, I'm Seo In Uk.

142
00:09:17,713 --> 00:09:21,279
These are the final three for Moo Gyeom.

143
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:24,095
Let's pick one.

144
00:09:25,898 --> 00:09:28,181
You came ready like you were waiting for this.

145
00:09:28,181 --> 00:09:30,138
I didn't find them.

146
00:09:30,138 --> 00:09:33,349
They wanted in before Sim Yu Geon.

147
00:09:33,349 --> 00:09:35,994
Is recasting really our best option?

148
00:09:35,994 --> 00:09:37,286
More than best.

149
00:09:37,286 --> 00:09:39,929
It may be for the better.

150
00:09:39,929 --> 00:09:40,973
Exactly.

151
00:09:40,973 --> 00:09:44,546
And he's the hottest actor in Korea right now.

152
00:09:44,546 --> 00:09:45,962
Geum Seong Moo.

153
00:09:45,962 --> 00:09:47,812
Geum Seong Moo?

154
00:09:48,490 --> 00:09:50,700
- Why?
- I mean...

155
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:53,177
If he's that hot, isn't he busy?

156
00:09:53,177 --> 00:09:55,214
He must have projects lined up.

157
00:09:55,214 --> 00:09:59,433
If the script is good, actors line up for it.

158
00:09:59,433 --> 00:10:01,278
You're too kind.

159
00:10:01,278 --> 00:10:02,718
So...

160
00:10:02,718 --> 00:10:03,781
Let's wrap this up.

161
00:10:03,781 --> 00:10:08,650
We're burning money as we speak.

162
00:10:08,650 --> 00:10:13,015
CEO An secured more funding in LA

163
00:10:13,015 --> 00:10:15,803
and even closed pre-sales.

164
00:10:15,803 --> 00:10:19,093
Doesn't that mean
this project means more to her now?

165
00:10:19,093 --> 00:10:20,237
Yeah.

166
00:10:20,237 --> 00:10:21,246
So?

167
00:10:21,246 --> 00:10:24,279
CEO An has no plans to drop Yu Geon.

168
00:10:25,152 --> 00:10:27,556
She used him as a bluff.

169
00:10:27,556 --> 00:10:30,412
For what?

170
00:10:43,631 --> 00:10:46,289
[Contract for Pop Culture Artists]

171
00:10:51,282 --> 00:10:54,139
You didn't call me here to end my contract?

172
00:10:54,139 --> 00:10:58,257
You really underestimated me.

173
00:10:58,257 --> 00:11:01,823
Did you think you could break this contract?

174
00:11:01,823 --> 00:11:03,847
Did you forget what I told you?

175
00:11:03,847 --> 00:11:07,921
That scrap of paper owns you, body and soul.

176
00:11:26,261 --> 00:11:28,459
I'll renew my contract.

177
00:11:28,459 --> 00:11:29,957
Leave Yu Geon alone.

178
00:11:29,957 --> 00:11:31,424
Good.

179
00:11:32,030 --> 00:11:35,004
Your contract is in his hand.

180
00:11:35,004 --> 00:11:37,607
- Stamp it.
- You don't have to do this.

181
00:11:37,607 --> 00:11:40,607
I'll put everything back the way it was.

182
00:11:42,341 --> 00:11:43,925
How?

183
00:11:43,925 --> 00:11:46,586
Are you naive, or just clueless?

184
00:11:46,586 --> 00:11:49,805
Mom wanted me from the start.

185
00:11:51,032 --> 00:11:52,456
And Mom,

186
00:11:52,456 --> 00:11:54,843
I wasn't doing this film because of him.

187
00:11:54,843 --> 00:11:57,885
I found the script myself.
I even auditioned for it.

188
00:11:57,885 --> 00:12:00,642
He just happened to be there after I joined.

189
00:12:00,642 --> 00:12:01,995
Annoyingly enough.

190
00:12:01,995 --> 00:12:04,509
Then I had good instincts.

191
00:12:04,509 --> 00:12:08,359
I picked the right hostage
and brought you back.

192
00:12:08,359 --> 00:12:10,483
Give her the contract.

193
00:12:10,483 --> 00:12:12,178
Give it to me.

194
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:31,846
I trust this paper more than your feelings.

195
00:12:32,453 --> 00:12:34,775
You're still in my palm.

196
00:12:34,775 --> 00:12:37,390
What can you possibly do?

197
00:12:44,487 --> 00:12:46,808
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

198
00:12:46,808 --> 00:12:51,951
Why did Nan Young risk her life
to save Moo Gyeom?

199
00:12:52,589 --> 00:12:54,539
She ran off to live as herself.

200
00:12:54,539 --> 00:12:56,359
What an idiot.

201
00:12:57,309 --> 00:13:00,615
Maybe that was how she saved herself.

202
00:13:00,615 --> 00:13:02,179
Ha Na.

203
00:13:02,179 --> 00:13:03,575
They say when you're in love,

204
00:13:03,575 --> 00:13:07,423
your eyes, nose, and lips
all turn toward that person.

205
00:13:07,423 --> 00:13:09,342
You know what that means?

206
00:13:09,342 --> 00:13:13,121
You look at their face more than your own.

207
00:13:13,121 --> 00:13:17,797
So when they smile, you smile too.

208
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:22,630
And when they cry, you realize you cry too.

209
00:13:24,807 --> 00:13:27,541
Is that why it hurts this much?

210
00:13:28,274 --> 00:13:30,011
Ha Na.

211
00:13:30,011 --> 00:13:32,768
I'm sorry, but please stop talking.

212
00:13:32,768 --> 00:13:36,675
We've gotten on Olympic Expressway
three times now.

213
00:13:37,729 --> 00:13:39,145
Gosh...

214
00:13:39,145 --> 00:13:41,639
Sorry. Can you pull over somewhere?

215
00:13:41,639 --> 00:13:42,843
I can't pull over.

216
00:13:42,843 --> 00:13:44,829
There are too many cars.

217
00:13:44,829 --> 00:13:48,052
I'm actually scared of driving.

218
00:13:49,010 --> 00:13:50,921
How much farther?

219
00:13:50,921 --> 00:13:53,561
Check the GPS, please.

220
00:13:55,141 --> 00:13:59,245
I think Crow should be played
by someone everyone knows.

221
00:13:59,245 --> 00:14:01,899
- Yeah.
- He's the independence army leader.

222
00:14:01,899 --> 00:14:03,929
His entrance needs impact.

223
00:14:03,929 --> 00:14:07,786
Someone who makes the audience gasp
the second they see him.

224
00:14:07,786 --> 00:14:10,111
But it's a small role, so it might be tough.

225
00:14:10,111 --> 00:14:13,651
Then why not offer it as a cameo?

226
00:14:13,651 --> 00:14:16,559
Is now really the time to discuss a cameo?

227
00:14:16,559 --> 00:14:18,046
We don't even have a lead.

228
00:14:18,046 --> 00:14:19,735
We should do what we can.

229
00:14:19,735 --> 00:14:21,324
You said we're burning money.

230
00:14:21,324 --> 00:14:23,877
The articles are out!

231
00:14:29,980 --> 00:14:31,911
[Who Is Sim Yu Geon, Oh Ha Na's Leading Man?]

232
00:14:31,911 --> 00:14:34,200
Topline released these.

233
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:36,315
Yu Geon got an article...

234
00:14:36,315 --> 00:14:38,420
We need an official release too.

235
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:40,483
- Get on it.
- Yes, sir.

236
00:14:43,526 --> 00:14:45,135
<i>Please help me.</i>

237
00:14:45,135 --> 00:14:47,991
<i>So I can live as Oh Ha Na, not her daughter.</i>

238
00:14:47,991 --> 00:14:51,409
<i>If Nan Young can be
my first step toward independence,</i>

239
00:14:51,409 --> 00:14:54,111
<i>it'll mean everything to me.</i>

240
00:14:55,497 --> 00:14:58,230
So her first step toward independence is gone.

241
00:14:58,230 --> 00:15:00,891
Will she be okay?

242
00:15:00,891 --> 00:15:02,898
She will be.

243
00:15:02,898 --> 00:15:05,581
Either way, she chose this herself.

244
00:15:05,581 --> 00:15:08,045
To protect what matters to her.

245
00:15:12,703 --> 00:15:14,456
[Who Is Sim Yu Geon, Oh Ha Na's Leading Man?]

246
00:15:14,456 --> 00:15:16,529
[Oh Ha Na Makes Her Film Debut
in Ian Woo's Next Project]

247
00:15:24,383 --> 00:15:26,690
[Expiration date: Ten thousand years]

248
00:15:32,702 --> 00:15:35,435
<i>You were desperate enough
to sign that insane contract.</i>

249
00:15:35,435 --> 00:15:38,452
<i>Why quit now?</i>

250
00:15:41,190 --> 00:15:45,571
<i>You should've stayed right by my side
and shown my mom properly.</i>

251
00:15:46,196 --> 00:15:48,736
<i>That there's absolutely no such thing as love.</i>

252
00:16:58,631 --> 00:17:01,317
Hwa Yeon!

253
00:17:07,591 --> 00:17:10,103
Hwa Yeon!

254
00:17:11,677 --> 00:17:15,438
If she's not here, where the hell is she?

255
00:17:20,492 --> 00:17:24,414
When I find you, you're dead!

256
00:17:28,146 --> 00:17:30,097
Woo Soo Bin!

257
00:17:30,097 --> 00:17:32,270
Woo Soo Bin!

258
00:17:34,342 --> 00:17:36,288
Woo Soo Bin!

259
00:17:53,385 --> 00:17:55,113
Evidence video.

260
00:17:55,113 --> 00:17:57,665
So no one thinks I did this.

261
00:18:01,790 --> 00:18:03,098
Long time no see.

262
00:18:03,098 --> 00:18:05,358
Yeah. 20 years.

263
00:18:05,358 --> 00:18:08,593
Get out in 20 seconds before I call the cops.

264
00:18:08,593 --> 00:18:13,363
An invited guest doesn't break down the door.

265
00:18:16,237 --> 00:18:18,780
Looks like the same goes for you.

266
00:18:20,469 --> 00:18:23,273
Coming to a house when no one's home.

267
00:18:23,273 --> 00:18:26,897
Why are you here anyway?

268
00:18:26,897 --> 00:18:31,131
I'm funding Soo Bin's movie.

269
00:18:31,131 --> 00:18:34,097
I had something urgent to discuss.

270
00:18:34,097 --> 00:18:35,973
What?

271
00:18:35,973 --> 00:18:37,075
Hey.

272
00:18:37,075 --> 00:18:39,953
You really are crazy.

273
00:18:39,953 --> 00:18:42,414
That's why I dated a bastard like you.

274
00:18:42,414 --> 00:18:43,957
I didn't even know you were married.

275
00:18:43,957 --> 00:18:45,568
Still bitter about that?

276
00:18:45,568 --> 00:18:48,086
You got pregnant
and told me to divorce my wife.

277
00:18:48,086 --> 00:18:50,506
You locked me in a clinic so I couldn't end it.

278
00:18:50,506 --> 00:18:52,903
Fine, fine.

279
00:18:52,903 --> 00:18:56,676
I made a huge mistake back then.

280
00:18:57,293 --> 00:19:02,129
You could've had the baby in secret...

281
00:19:02,129 --> 00:19:04,520
and disappeared.

282
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:06,898
No one would've cared.

283
00:19:07,576 --> 00:19:11,209
But I showed you useless mercy.

284
00:19:16,156 --> 00:19:19,956
That's how much I liked you.

285
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:23,423
Su Hui.

286
00:19:23,423 --> 00:19:26,148
I'll repay that kindness!

287
00:19:39,631 --> 00:19:41,328
Nice.

288
00:19:41,328 --> 00:19:43,710
Brings back memories.

289
00:19:57,937 --> 00:20:00,367
- I can't wait to get back on set.
- You like it that much?

290
00:20:00,367 --> 00:20:03,665
Of course. It's so much fun.

291
00:20:03,665 --> 00:20:05,013
Yeah?

292
00:20:08,145 --> 00:20:10,025
What is this?

293
00:20:11,579 --> 00:20:13,497
Wait here.

294
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:21,013
I should've had you thrown in jail back then!

295
00:20:22,392 --> 00:20:25,244
What are you two doing here?

296
00:20:26,899 --> 00:20:28,558
Yi Jae. Go home.

297
00:20:28,558 --> 00:20:30,131
Okay.

298
00:20:31,598 --> 00:20:33,539
Oh my...

299
00:20:36,149 --> 00:20:38,339
Where's your mom?

300
00:20:38,339 --> 00:20:41,092
I told you clearly.

301
00:20:41,092 --> 00:20:42,836
Don't look for her again.

302
00:20:42,836 --> 00:20:45,715
This time, you'll answer.

303
00:20:45,715 --> 00:20:48,301
Where's your mom?

304
00:20:51,145 --> 00:20:52,645
Hey.

305
00:20:58,223 --> 00:20:59,258
Are you insane?

306
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:02,221
It's attempted murder!

307
00:21:03,970 --> 00:21:06,486
Get out. Both of you.

308
00:21:08,081 --> 00:21:10,651
You said you'd be a stain on my life forever.

309
00:21:10,651 --> 00:21:12,281
And this is your plan?

310
00:21:12,281 --> 00:21:15,124
Siding with the mom who abandoned you?

311
00:21:15,124 --> 00:21:17,748
Have you no shame?

312
00:21:18,431 --> 00:21:21,994
What the hell is this scumbag saying?

313
00:21:21,994 --> 00:21:24,451
I never spent a day as his mom.

314
00:21:24,451 --> 00:21:26,911
So don't call me that.

315
00:21:26,911 --> 00:21:29,195
I came here as Ha Na's mom.

316
00:21:29,195 --> 00:21:31,375
Exactly.

317
00:21:31,375 --> 00:21:33,809
So get out.

318
00:21:33,809 --> 00:21:36,764
Neither of you is anything to me.

319
00:21:37,696 --> 00:21:39,463
Then...

320
00:21:40,376 --> 00:21:44,137
You'll make Hwa Yeon
live on the run forever too?

321
00:21:44,137 --> 00:21:46,783
Just like you?

322
00:21:46,783 --> 00:21:50,800
She's not running.
I'm keeping her safe from you.

323
00:22:07,578 --> 00:22:12,423
If you don't want her hurt,
send her back to me.

324
00:22:20,713 --> 00:22:23,786
I shouldn't have fixed you.

325
00:22:24,547 --> 00:22:28,177
Things that are broken once

326
00:22:28,177 --> 00:22:32,137
- are hard to fix completely...
- Father!

327
00:22:33,419 --> 00:22:34,563
You're right.

328
00:22:34,563 --> 00:22:39,806
Just because you fixed my leg
doesn't mean you fixed my life.

329
00:22:39,806 --> 00:22:45,012
Soo Bin is the one
who put my life back together.

330
00:23:02,271 --> 00:23:04,893
That bastard still lives like that?

331
00:23:04,893 --> 00:23:08,637
And you still live like this?

332
00:23:08,637 --> 00:23:11,684
I didn't come here to watch this mess.

333
00:23:11,684 --> 00:23:13,810
Hey.

334
00:23:13,810 --> 00:23:16,881
Why did you cast Ha Na?

335
00:23:16,881 --> 00:23:20,254
You came all this way to ask me that?

336
00:23:20,254 --> 00:23:23,588
What did you think I was after?

337
00:23:23,588 --> 00:23:26,978
You wouldn't take her when I offered.

338
00:23:26,978 --> 00:23:31,051
So why cast her the moment she left me?

339
00:23:32,214 --> 00:23:36,790
You and my father really are alike.

340
00:23:36,790 --> 00:23:39,188
- What?
- Maybe that's why

341
00:23:39,188 --> 00:23:41,401
Ha Na and I are alike.

342
00:23:41,401 --> 00:23:43,088
Though we weren't raised together.

343
00:23:43,088 --> 00:23:44,125
Hey!

344
00:23:44,125 --> 00:23:46,682
That's exactly why I came here.

345
00:23:46,682 --> 00:23:52,454
Don't you dare tell Ha Na
you're siblings or family.

346
00:23:52,454 --> 00:23:54,479
Or I don't know what I'll do.

347
00:23:54,479 --> 00:23:58,607
A director cast an actress in a movie.

348
00:23:59,202 --> 00:24:01,674
You're reading a lot into it.

349
00:24:02,408 --> 00:24:05,444
This is an important time for her.

350
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:08,478
So don't get swept up in pointless emotions.

351
00:24:08,478 --> 00:24:12,294
Just finish the movie.

352
00:24:34,331 --> 00:24:35,795
Soo Bin.

353
00:24:35,795 --> 00:24:37,742
Are you okay?

354
00:24:39,136 --> 00:24:41,729
Yi Jae, I'm sorry.

355
00:24:42,802 --> 00:24:44,475
Give me a minute.

356
00:25:23,310 --> 00:25:25,053
Woo Soo Bin.

357
00:25:56,305 --> 00:25:59,727
They say all happy families are alike,

358
00:25:59,727 --> 00:26:01,950
but every unhappy family

359
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:05,123
has its own reason.

360
00:26:05,123 --> 00:26:06,454
<i>Hello.</i>

361
00:26:06,454 --> 00:26:08,235
<i>You must be Soo Bin.</i>

362
00:26:08,235 --> 00:26:09,698
<i>Say hello.</i>

363
00:26:09,698 --> 00:26:13,065
<i>This is your aunt and your uncle.</i>

364
00:26:13,065 --> 00:26:14,490
<i>Hello.</i>

365
00:26:14,490 --> 00:26:16,546
In our family,

366
00:26:16,546 --> 00:26:18,257
I was that reason.

367
00:26:25,916 --> 00:26:27,629
<i>It's An Su Hui.</i>

368
00:26:31,368 --> 00:26:33,175
<i>Look.</i>

369
00:26:33,175 --> 00:26:36,466
<i>He looks more like her every day.</i>

370
00:26:36,466 --> 00:26:39,264
<i>So she really is his mom?</i>

371
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:42,589
<i>Her husband really is...</i>

372
00:26:43,209 --> 00:26:45,520
<i>Hwa Yeon is something else.</i>

373
00:26:45,520 --> 00:26:49,516
<i>Raising a child from his affair...</i>

374
00:26:49,516 --> 00:26:51,566
<i>So damn ignorant.</i>

375
00:26:51,566 --> 00:26:54,528
<i>Why would you say that crap to a kid?</i>

376
00:26:54,528 --> 00:26:56,986
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

377
00:26:56,986 --> 00:26:59,278
<i>I'm sorry...</i>

378
00:27:00,050 --> 00:27:04,355
<i>Soo Bin is my son.</i>

379
00:27:08,775 --> 00:27:12,818
<i>If you want your family that badly, go alone.</i>

380
00:27:12,818 --> 00:27:15,426
<i>And don't come back.</i>

381
00:27:16,039 --> 00:27:18,599
<i>No...</i>

382
00:27:19,359 --> 00:27:22,232
<i>I won't go again.</i>

383
00:27:22,845 --> 00:27:24,747
<i>I mean it.</i>

384
00:27:28,065 --> 00:27:29,877
That was when I realized.

385
00:27:32,148 --> 00:27:33,195
Some smiles...

386
00:27:33,195 --> 00:27:36,262
<i>Sweetie. You're awake?</i>

387
00:27:36,262 --> 00:27:38,462
look like crying.

388
00:27:39,952 --> 00:27:43,013
Every time Mom looked at me,

389
00:27:43,013 --> 00:27:44,977
she was crying.

390
00:28:04,867 --> 00:28:06,430
<i>Hey.</i>

391
00:28:12,264 --> 00:28:14,927
<i>Mom, who is he?</i>

392
00:28:17,487 --> 00:28:18,750
<i>Ha Na.</i>

393
00:28:18,750 --> 00:28:20,763
<i>Get inside!</i>

394
00:28:29,538 --> 00:28:31,271
<i>Who are you?</i>

395
00:28:32,099 --> 00:28:35,225
<i>Hello. I'm Woo Soo Bin.</i>

396
00:28:41,568 --> 00:28:43,298
<i>What are you doing here?</i>

397
00:28:43,298 --> 00:28:45,136
<i>Who sent you?</i>

398
00:28:45,136 --> 00:28:47,875
<i>Woo Cheol Gyu? Or that woman?</i>

399
00:28:47,875 --> 00:28:48,894
<i>What?</i>

400
00:28:48,894 --> 00:28:50,415
<i>They don't want you anymore?</i>

401
00:28:50,415 --> 00:28:51,770
<i>I came alone.</i>

402
00:28:51,770 --> 00:28:54,577
<i>My mom cries every day because of me.</i>

403
00:28:54,577 --> 00:28:58,864
<i>If I'm gone, Dad won't get mad,
and Mom won't cry.</i>

404
00:28:58,864 --> 00:29:00,181
<i>So what?</i>

405
00:29:00,181 --> 00:29:02,327
<i>Please raise me.</i>

406
00:29:02,327 --> 00:29:04,852
<i>I'm good at school. I listen well.</i>

407
00:29:04,852 --> 00:29:09,340
<i>If you just raise me, I'll grow up well.</i>

408
00:29:09,340 --> 00:29:12,173
<i>- Where's your house? Lead the way.
- No!</i>

409
00:29:12,173 --> 00:29:14,671
<i>Please take me in!</i>

410
00:29:14,671 --> 00:29:16,753
<i>- Keep it down!
- Please!</i>

411
00:29:16,753 --> 00:29:18,511
<i>Please.</i>

412
00:29:18,511 --> 00:29:20,995
<i>- Quiet!
- Please take me in...</i>

413
00:29:20,995 --> 00:29:23,426
<i>Please.</i>

414
00:29:23,426 --> 00:29:25,751
<i>Please take me in...</i>

415
00:29:26,912 --> 00:29:28,735
<i>Oh my...</i>

416
00:29:28,735 --> 00:29:30,992
<i>Please take me in...</i>

417
00:29:30,992 --> 00:29:33,181
<i>- Stop it.
- Please.</i>

418
00:29:45,475 --> 00:29:46,902
<i>Get out.</i>

419
00:29:52,264 --> 00:29:55,081
<i>This is why he came to me!</i>

420
00:29:55,081 --> 00:29:56,518
<i>He begged me to take him in.</i>

421
00:29:56,518 --> 00:29:57,824
<i>Can you believe it?</i>

422
00:29:57,824 --> 00:29:59,151
<i>Great.</i>

423
00:29:59,151 --> 00:30:00,801
<i>Then you raise him.</i>

424
00:30:00,801 --> 00:30:03,941
<i>I don't need this rotten kid either.</i>

425
00:30:03,941 --> 00:30:06,656
<i>Cheol Gyu! I have my own family now.</i>

426
00:30:06,656 --> 00:30:09,451
<i>How am I supposed to raise him?</i>

427
00:30:09,451 --> 00:30:12,760
<i>- Mom...
- I'm not your mom!</i>

428
00:30:12,760 --> 00:30:15,083
<i>Come here, Soo Bin.</i>

429
00:30:20,033 --> 00:30:23,263
<i>Where did you go?</i>

430
00:30:23,263 --> 00:30:26,956
<i>Do you know how worried I was?</i>

431
00:30:26,956 --> 00:30:28,743
<i>I just...</i>

432
00:30:28,743 --> 00:30:32,449
<i>I thought I was the reason you cried.</i>

433
00:30:33,847 --> 00:30:35,834
<i>Soo Bin...</i>

434
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:38,169
<i>You make me cry,</i>

435
00:30:38,169 --> 00:30:41,937
<i>and you make me smile like this too.</i>

436
00:30:41,937 --> 00:30:44,220
<i>Because you're my son.</i>

437
00:30:48,030 --> 00:30:49,761
<i>Mom...</i>

438
00:30:49,761 --> 00:30:52,470
<i>Don't cry, my son.</i>

439
00:31:10,386 --> 00:31:12,832
After that day...

440
00:31:12,832 --> 00:31:16,103
my whole world was just pitch-black darkness.

441
00:31:22,756 --> 00:31:26,040
When I thought I was better off in the dark...

442
00:31:29,216 --> 00:31:31,259
That's when I met you.

443
00:31:34,506 --> 00:31:37,492
Why does this story end with you?

444
00:31:38,326 --> 00:31:40,020
Maybe...

445
00:31:40,839 --> 00:31:43,602
Because you were the first person

446
00:31:44,195 --> 00:31:46,242
who lit up my world.

447
00:31:48,659 --> 00:31:50,292
Woo Soo Bin.

448
00:31:51,983 --> 00:31:54,603
Because of you...

449
00:31:54,603 --> 00:31:59,333
all my bad memories turned into love.

450
00:32:00,583 --> 00:32:06,069
This scar now means I loved you that much.

451
00:32:06,069 --> 00:32:10,929
And movies aren't some dream
I never got to have.

452
00:32:10,929 --> 00:32:13,774
They're a dream I share with you.

453
00:32:15,617 --> 00:32:17,817
When it rains...

454
00:32:19,731 --> 00:32:22,687
I don't think of our breakup anymore.

455
00:32:22,687 --> 00:32:25,440
I think of our kiss.

456
00:32:28,320 --> 00:32:32,929
How could this not be love?

457
00:32:38,500 --> 00:32:42,978
That's the greatest comfort I've ever had.

458
00:32:42,978 --> 00:32:44,670
Really?

459
00:33:49,178 --> 00:33:51,081
Sorry.

460
00:33:51,081 --> 00:33:54,230
It's been so long since someone was next to me.

461
00:33:57,230 --> 00:33:58,880
What?

462
00:33:58,880 --> 00:34:00,250
What time is it?

463
00:34:00,250 --> 00:34:02,254
Can I sleep a little longer?

464
00:34:03,537 --> 00:34:05,226
"So long?"

465
00:34:07,982 --> 00:34:10,382
Wake me up later.

466
00:34:12,704 --> 00:34:15,055
"So long?"

467
00:34:15,055 --> 00:34:17,062
I don't know.

468
00:34:20,346 --> 00:34:21,431
How long has it been?

469
00:34:21,431 --> 00:34:24,951
Why are you doing this so early?

470
00:34:24,951 --> 00:34:28,504
I said, how long has it been?

471
00:34:28,504 --> 00:34:29,931
- I don't know.
- Hey.

472
00:34:29,931 --> 00:34:31,621
- Ju Yi Jae!
- Yeah?

473
00:34:31,621 --> 00:34:33,491
- Was it him?
- Huh?

474
00:34:33,491 --> 00:34:36,487
- I'm asking you.
- That tickles.

475
00:34:36,487 --> 00:34:38,654
- Answer me.
- It tickles!

476
00:34:43,125 --> 00:34:46,149
That war-zone love guy?

477
00:34:46,872 --> 00:34:48,420
Right?

478
00:34:50,598 --> 00:34:53,515
He was good at cutting apples too.

479
00:34:53,515 --> 00:34:54,895
What?

480
00:34:58,102 --> 00:35:00,032
How good?

481
00:35:00,032 --> 00:35:02,350
Could he make apple bunnies too?

482
00:35:03,705 --> 00:35:05,176
Today's finally the scene.

483
00:35:05,176 --> 00:35:07,441
Nan Young falls for Moo Gyeom at first sight.

484
00:35:07,441 --> 00:35:09,127
I can't wait.

485
00:35:09,127 --> 00:35:12,196
Why? Did you fall for him at first sight too?

486
00:35:12,196 --> 00:35:14,573
How long are you keeping this up?

487
00:35:14,573 --> 00:35:15,985
When are you going to tell me?

488
00:35:15,985 --> 00:35:19,258
I told you, we only dated for a bit.

489
00:35:19,258 --> 00:35:21,848
He was an acting major...

490
00:35:21,848 --> 00:35:24,111
So he was hot.

491
00:35:24,111 --> 00:35:25,882
Of course.

492
00:35:26,752 --> 00:35:29,376
He was cute back then. Not now.

493
00:35:29,376 --> 00:35:32,485
You still keep in touch?

494
00:35:32,485 --> 00:35:34,468
No, no!

495
00:35:34,468 --> 00:35:40,286
We just dated in college,
so we had mutual friends.

496
00:35:40,286 --> 00:35:43,556
Anyway, he kept helping me on my student films.

497
00:35:43,556 --> 00:35:45,676
It just happened. That's all.

498
00:35:45,676 --> 00:35:48,440
"It just happened?" That's the dangerous part.

499
00:35:48,440 --> 00:35:51,793
Must not have meant much if I barely remember.

500
00:35:51,793 --> 00:35:54,483
You said it was life-or-death.
Did you kill him?

501
00:35:54,483 --> 00:35:56,459
Just tell me.

502
00:35:57,365 --> 00:35:59,389
Fine. I killed him.

503
00:35:59,389 --> 00:36:01,154
Brutally.

504
00:36:03,659 --> 00:36:04,916
Wait.

505
00:36:04,916 --> 00:36:06,708
Am I the only one with a past?

506
00:36:06,708 --> 00:36:08,390
I don't have one.

507
00:36:08,390 --> 00:36:11,013
- Really?
- Even if I did, I wouldn't tell you.

508
00:36:11,013 --> 00:36:13,038
It's called respect.

509
00:36:13,038 --> 00:36:15,929
So now I'm the rude one?

510
00:36:15,929 --> 00:36:17,594
You kept asking.

511
00:36:17,594 --> 00:36:20,457
Because you kept spilling.

512
00:36:23,286 --> 00:36:25,630
- But really? No one?
- I said no.

513
00:36:25,630 --> 00:36:28,430
- Was she prettier than me?
- Be careful.

514
00:36:29,642 --> 00:36:31,259
[No Dating on Set]
Morning, sir.

515
00:36:31,259 --> 00:36:33,213
- Hello.
- Hello.

516
00:36:33,872 --> 00:36:35,814
- Hello.
- Hello.

517
00:36:35,814 --> 00:36:37,920
Good morning.

518
00:36:37,920 --> 00:36:39,680
What are you doing?

519
00:36:39,680 --> 00:36:42,244
We've already caught three couples.

520
00:36:42,244 --> 00:36:45,710
They should be working, not dating!

521
00:36:47,397 --> 00:36:49,327
Four couples, actually...

522
00:36:50,397 --> 00:36:53,967
A set with lots of couples has good energy.

523
00:36:53,967 --> 00:36:56,470
Who says that?

524
00:36:56,470 --> 00:36:58,685
It's only good for them.

525
00:36:58,685 --> 00:37:03,588
If you ever catch the staff dating,
report it to us right away.

526
00:37:03,588 --> 00:37:05,901
See you later.

527
00:37:14,595 --> 00:37:17,016
[No Smoking on Set]
[No Dating on Set]

528
00:37:41,397 --> 00:37:43,086
"And then...

529
00:37:43,086 --> 00:37:45,096
I fell in love..."

530
00:38:09,664 --> 00:38:12,118
You're about to drool.

531
00:38:12,806 --> 00:38:15,616
Change the way you look at Nan Young.

532
00:38:15,616 --> 00:38:18,127
No lovesick eyes yet.

533
00:38:18,127 --> 00:38:19,486
What?

534
00:38:19,486 --> 00:38:21,824
I'm not. Yi Jae...

535
00:38:21,824 --> 00:38:22,667
Director Ju.

536
00:38:22,667 --> 00:38:25,355
Drop all the worry, fear, and pain.

537
00:38:25,355 --> 00:38:27,700
You're Moo Gyeom, the carefree young master.

538
00:38:27,700 --> 00:38:28,926
Not an independence fighter.

539
00:38:28,926 --> 00:38:30,388
Got it?

540
00:38:31,785 --> 00:38:33,897
Please keep up the good work.

541
00:38:33,897 --> 00:38:35,972
Thank you.

542
00:38:38,135 --> 00:38:39,446
Moo Gyeom.

543
00:38:39,446 --> 00:38:41,245
Let's talk.

544
00:38:42,824 --> 00:38:44,988
- Hurry.
- Okay.

545
00:38:46,397 --> 00:38:48,981
How are you feeling? You okay?

546
00:38:48,981 --> 00:38:51,084
Of course.

547
00:38:51,084 --> 00:38:52,867
Director Ju.

548
00:38:53,741 --> 00:38:57,518
Even if I went back to where I was,

549
00:38:57,518 --> 00:39:00,188
I'm not the old Oh Ha Na anymore.

550
00:39:00,188 --> 00:39:02,731
I've been reborn.

551
00:39:02,731 --> 00:39:04,083
Life, round two.

552
00:39:04,083 --> 00:39:06,268
Happy birthday.

553
00:39:06,268 --> 00:39:09,238
Even if Nan Young runs out of Wolhajeong,

554
00:39:09,238 --> 00:39:14,021
it means nothing
if Moo Gyeom isn't in that world.

555
00:39:14,021 --> 00:39:17,958
That's why she threw herself in
to save him, right?

556
00:39:17,958 --> 00:39:19,195
Right.

557
00:39:19,195 --> 00:39:23,529
I signed that contract to protect myself.

558
00:39:30,579 --> 00:39:32,372
Come closer.

559
00:39:32,372 --> 00:39:34,451
Who was Yi Jae's ex?

560
00:39:34,451 --> 00:39:36,977
What? Yi Jae's ex?

561
00:39:37,766 --> 00:39:39,986
Keep your voice down.

562
00:39:39,986 --> 00:39:42,069
Which ex, exactly?

563
00:39:42,069 --> 00:39:45,215
- There was more than one?
- Of course.

564
00:39:45,215 --> 00:39:47,655
Just the ones I know...

565
00:39:54,911 --> 00:39:56,486
Enough.

566
00:39:58,686 --> 00:40:02,238
One of them got really famous...

567
00:40:09,243 --> 00:40:10,820
No.

568
00:40:11,922 --> 00:40:13,730
I don't want to know.

569
00:40:14,349 --> 00:40:16,104
What's with him?

570
00:40:35,799 --> 00:40:37,383
That's the look.

571
00:40:37,383 --> 00:40:39,348
Love at first sight.

572
00:40:39,348 --> 00:40:41,251
- Sorry?
- Let's rehearse.

573
00:40:41,251 --> 00:40:43,771
Let's rehearse!

574
00:40:45,862 --> 00:40:47,388
So...

575
00:40:48,301 --> 00:40:49,685
Let's do it.

576
00:40:49,685 --> 00:40:51,288
- Okay.
- Okay.

577
00:40:53,176 --> 00:40:55,116
Ready.

578
00:40:55,116 --> 00:40:56,667
Action!

579
00:40:56,667 --> 00:40:58,476
I don't believe we've met.

580
00:40:58,476 --> 00:41:00,976
I'm Nan Young.

581
00:41:05,323 --> 00:41:07,027
What are you doing?

582
00:41:07,027 --> 00:41:09,290
Grab my wrist.

583
00:41:13,127 --> 00:41:15,922
Too proper. You're not a scholar.

584
00:41:17,700 --> 00:41:19,114
Read it again.

585
00:41:19,114 --> 00:41:21,397
Memorize the action lines too.

586
00:41:22,113 --> 00:41:24,064
Sorry.

587
00:41:24,064 --> 00:41:25,979
I'm sorry.

588
00:41:27,446 --> 00:41:29,992
- Sorry.
- It's okay.

589
00:41:29,992 --> 00:41:31,965
- What do we do?
- Sorry.

590
00:41:31,965 --> 00:41:34,165
Let them work it out.

591
00:41:35,107 --> 00:41:37,319
Let's go again.

592
00:41:37,319 --> 00:41:39,864
Focus a little more, please.

593
00:41:39,864 --> 00:41:41,614
Ready...

594
00:41:41,614 --> 00:41:43,158
Action!

595
00:41:44,546 --> 00:41:47,157
I don't believe we've met.

596
00:41:47,157 --> 00:41:49,710
I'm Nan Young.

597
00:41:57,219 --> 00:42:01,469
Noble young master, you're quite impatient.

598
00:42:01,469 --> 00:42:04,048
Why shouldn't I be?

599
00:42:04,736 --> 00:42:09,022
When your eyes are so full of love for me.

600
00:42:12,245 --> 00:42:14,169
Relax a little.

601
00:42:14,169 --> 00:42:15,465
Cut! Great!

602
00:42:15,465 --> 00:42:17,751
Let's go with that.

603
00:42:39,409 --> 00:42:41,770
<i>The spa date is over.</i>

604
00:42:41,770 --> 00:42:44,628
<i>Of the two people you dated today,</i>

605
00:42:44,628 --> 00:42:48,343
<i>go to the room of the one you like more.</i>

606
00:43:32,946 --> 00:43:34,847
Seo In Uk.

607
00:43:36,973 --> 00:43:39,783
I don't sleep with a guy twice
after a drunken hookup.

608
00:43:39,783 --> 00:43:42,182
Some might call it a stupid rule,

609
00:43:42,182 --> 00:43:46,184
but I've lived by it.

610
00:43:47,346 --> 00:43:49,686
But just now...

611
00:43:49,686 --> 00:43:54,233
we had our second night.

612
00:43:54,233 --> 00:43:56,450
What do you think that means?

613
00:43:56,450 --> 00:43:59,310
That there'll be a third.

614
00:43:59,310 --> 00:44:01,097
Maybe even more.

615
00:44:06,177 --> 00:44:07,808
Okay.

616
00:44:07,808 --> 00:44:10,408
- I'll leave the show.
- No.

617
00:44:10,408 --> 00:44:12,432
Don't.

618
00:44:12,432 --> 00:44:13,465
Sorry?

619
00:44:13,465 --> 00:44:18,050
Our third time will be after this shoot wraps.

620
00:44:18,050 --> 00:44:22,110
So stay the game changer until the end.

621
00:44:23,946 --> 00:44:26,415
The man everyone wants.

622
00:44:28,039 --> 00:44:30,059
What does that even mean?

623
00:44:30,059 --> 00:44:32,035
Five minutes left.

624
00:44:32,681 --> 00:44:35,485
Enjoy your date.

625
00:44:43,392 --> 00:44:46,020
She's so weird.

626
00:44:47,578 --> 00:44:48,998
I love it.

627
00:44:49,678 --> 00:44:52,275
Please wrap everything up within 30 minutes!

628
00:44:52,275 --> 00:44:53,042
- Got it.
- Got it.

629
00:44:53,042 --> 00:44:55,839
The team dinner is optional,
so feel free to join if you'd like.

630
00:44:55,839 --> 00:44:56,850
- Yes.
- Yes.

631
00:44:56,850 --> 00:44:58,894
I shared the location in the group chat.

632
00:44:58,894 --> 00:45:01,621
- Please check it!
- Okay!

633
00:45:04,112 --> 00:45:05,176
Directors!

634
00:45:05,176 --> 00:45:10,762
Geum Seong Moo agreed to make a cameo as Crow!

635
00:45:10,762 --> 00:45:12,942
Isn't that amazing?

636
00:45:15,553 --> 00:45:18,676
What? Geum Seong Moo?

637
00:45:18,676 --> 00:45:20,931
That's great.

638
00:45:20,931 --> 00:45:22,206
Oh, right.

639
00:45:22,206 --> 00:45:23,242
Director Ryu.

640
00:45:23,242 --> 00:45:25,502
What I mentioned earlier...

641
00:45:26,829 --> 00:45:29,149
I don't think this is good news.

642
00:45:32,065 --> 00:45:34,265
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

643
00:45:44,933 --> 00:45:46,463
Is the beer good?

644
00:45:46,463 --> 00:45:49,616
Just have one. You'll be fine.

645
00:45:50,904 --> 00:45:53,490
I'll stick to soda.

646
00:46:04,091 --> 00:46:06,064
- Did you see that?
- What?

647
00:46:16,102 --> 00:46:19,046
So Geum Seong Moo is really doing the cameo?

648
00:46:19,046 --> 00:46:22,214
- Why?
- We did a drama together.

649
00:46:22,214 --> 00:46:25,226
I'm not sure he fits Crow.

650
00:46:25,226 --> 00:46:27,777
Guess you had beef with him too.

651
00:46:27,777 --> 00:46:28,439
What?

652
00:46:28,439 --> 00:46:31,303
I hear you always have issues
with male co-stars.

653
00:46:31,303 --> 00:46:33,601
Getting along with them is part of the job.

654
00:46:33,601 --> 00:46:36,854
Jeez... You sound just like my mom.

655
00:46:38,998 --> 00:46:42,241
If he were easy to get along with, I would've.

656
00:46:42,241 --> 00:46:45,598
What am I, some thug picking fights everywhere?

657
00:46:45,598 --> 00:46:48,422
She gets along with Yu Geon.

658
00:46:49,363 --> 00:46:52,013
You've already had six pieces.

659
00:46:52,727 --> 00:46:54,781
You need to watch yourself during shoots.

660
00:46:54,781 --> 00:46:57,392
You think good genes last forever?

661
00:46:57,392 --> 00:46:58,978
Yes, ma'am.

662
00:46:58,978 --> 00:47:01,564
That damn "ma'am."

663
00:47:01,564 --> 00:47:03,213
You call that getting along?

664
00:47:03,213 --> 00:47:05,158
Seems sweet to her.

665
00:47:05,960 --> 00:47:08,306
Lucky you, Yu Geon.

666
00:47:08,306 --> 00:47:10,641
You love Seong Moo.

667
00:47:15,002 --> 00:47:16,503
You mean the Hong Kong actor, huh?

668
00:47:16,503 --> 00:47:20,334
His Korean name is Geum Seong Moo too...

669
00:47:21,239 --> 00:47:22,370
So what?

670
00:47:22,370 --> 00:47:25,074
I meant the Korean actor, Geum Seong Moo.

671
00:47:25,074 --> 00:47:27,832
- Is that his real name?
- Yeah, it is.

672
00:47:30,920 --> 00:47:32,423
You know him well?

673
00:47:32,423 --> 00:47:36,020
Oh, are you a fan of his too?

674
00:47:36,775 --> 00:47:38,677
That hurts.

675
00:47:38,677 --> 00:47:42,096
"Contract Marriage" aired against his
and got crushed in ratings.

676
00:47:42,096 --> 00:47:43,920
Oh, right.

677
00:47:43,920 --> 00:47:46,900
He's huge right now because of that drama.

678
00:47:46,900 --> 00:47:49,933
Everybody loves him.

679
00:47:50,853 --> 00:47:53,033
Lucky you.

680
00:47:53,033 --> 00:47:54,841
Let's keep work and feelings separate.

681
00:47:54,841 --> 00:47:56,667
You seem the worst at that.

682
00:47:56,667 --> 00:47:59,281
And you're so good at it?

683
00:48:02,004 --> 00:48:04,944
I'm trying, ma'am.

684
00:48:06,798 --> 00:48:09,135
I should go.

685
00:48:11,197 --> 00:48:13,309
Let's go, Chae Yeon.

686
00:48:18,680 --> 00:48:20,966
Why did she even come to dinner?

687
00:48:20,966 --> 00:48:22,718
To pick a fight, apparently.

688
00:48:22,718 --> 00:48:25,668
Moo Gyeom! Have a drink with me.

689
00:48:25,668 --> 00:48:27,836
That's okay, right?

690
00:48:27,836 --> 00:48:29,947
Have a little.

691
00:48:29,947 --> 00:48:31,691
Just a little.

692
00:48:31,691 --> 00:48:34,401
I'll drink a lot.

693
00:48:34,401 --> 00:48:36,337
Cheers!

694
00:48:45,183 --> 00:48:47,487
A little would've been fine...

695
00:48:47,487 --> 00:48:49,487
Another soju, please!

696
00:48:56,660 --> 00:48:59,077
Sim Yu Geon.

697
00:48:59,077 --> 00:49:02,178
Even I'm naturally gifted,
and I still work hard.

698
00:49:03,038 --> 00:49:07,000
You think this dewy glow maintains itself?

699
00:49:28,827 --> 00:49:31,239
He even drank?

700
00:49:37,904 --> 00:49:40,274
- Good night!
- Bye.

701
00:49:43,314 --> 00:49:44,321
<i>Want to take a walk?</i>

702
00:49:44,321 --> 00:49:48,352
Any couple I catch
sneaking out tonight is dead meat.

703
00:49:51,222 --> 00:49:53,246
<i>I'll come to your room later.</i>

704
00:49:53,246 --> 00:49:55,687
A walk is at least innocent.

705
00:49:55,687 --> 00:49:58,703
Patrol the halls.

706
00:49:58,703 --> 00:50:00,311
Exactly.

707
00:50:00,311 --> 00:50:04,322
There's definitely a couple on our floor.

708
00:50:04,322 --> 00:50:06,042
Really?

709
00:50:06,949 --> 00:50:08,759
Sharp.

710
00:50:08,759 --> 00:50:11,319
Ye Seo, you take the lower floors.

711
00:50:11,319 --> 00:50:13,093
I'll take upstairs.

712
00:50:13,093 --> 00:50:14,922
Me?

713
00:50:14,922 --> 00:50:16,985
No, thanks.

714
00:50:16,985 --> 00:50:19,662
I thought you were anti-dating.

715
00:50:19,662 --> 00:50:21,982
I'm against it,

716
00:50:21,982 --> 00:50:25,735
but you can't just tell love to stop.

717
00:50:25,735 --> 00:50:27,826
Right... Leave them.

718
00:50:27,826 --> 00:50:30,419
They'll break up when filming wraps.

719
00:50:30,419 --> 00:50:35,703
Exactly. Then why date at work
if they'll break up anyway?

720
00:50:35,703 --> 00:50:37,883
I won't let anyone off.

721
00:50:38,852 --> 00:50:40,236
- Good night!
- Good night.

722
00:50:40,236 --> 00:50:41,857
- Rest up.
- Yeah.

723
00:50:41,857 --> 00:50:44,516
- Good night.
- Sleep tight.

724
00:50:45,498 --> 00:50:47,591
<i>The doors are closing.</i>

725
00:50:48,305 --> 00:50:49,885
Hey.

726
00:50:50,858 --> 00:50:52,615
He looks wasted.

727
00:50:52,615 --> 00:50:54,562
Shouldn't we walk him to his room?

728
00:50:54,562 --> 00:50:56,346
Is he a kid?

729
00:50:56,346 --> 00:50:58,700
Sim Yu Geon. What floor?

730
00:50:58,700 --> 00:51:01,492
- Sixth.
- Seriously...

731
00:51:01,492 --> 00:51:03,879
- Let's go.
- Hey!

732
00:51:07,878 --> 00:51:09,820
Woo Soo Bin...

733
00:51:09,820 --> 00:51:12,987
You're dead when Seong Moo gets here.

734
00:51:22,724 --> 00:51:25,443
Wait! The keycard!

735
00:51:25,443 --> 00:51:27,231
I have it.

736
00:52:57,969 --> 00:53:00,462
Why won't it open...

737
00:53:01,872 --> 00:53:03,648
Come on.

738
00:53:12,149 --> 00:53:14,049
A ghost?

739
00:53:27,570 --> 00:53:30,390
That's your transit card.

740
00:53:30,390 --> 00:53:32,462
Where's your keycard?

741
00:53:34,654 --> 00:53:36,424
Is this a dream?

742
00:53:36,424 --> 00:53:38,144
Move.

743
00:53:52,006 --> 00:53:53,837
I'm sorry.

744
00:53:56,612 --> 00:53:59,671
There's so much I want to say...

745
00:54:01,787 --> 00:54:04,226
But this is all I can say.

746
00:54:04,226 --> 00:54:05,916
Sorry.

747
00:54:09,642 --> 00:54:12,448
What else do you want to say?

748
00:54:15,130 --> 00:54:17,304
I like you.

749
00:54:21,208 --> 00:54:24,038
Even saying that hurts.

750
00:54:26,096 --> 00:54:28,802
Guess I'm really paying for it.

751
00:54:35,705 --> 00:54:40,459
You won't remember this, will you?

752
00:54:40,459 --> 00:54:44,552
Do you want me to?

753
00:54:47,461 --> 00:54:49,595
Tell me to, and I will.

754
00:54:50,412 --> 00:54:53,085
Tell me not to, and I won't.

755
00:55:01,813 --> 00:55:03,750
I know

756
00:55:04,424 --> 00:55:07,321
there's something between us.

757
00:55:08,099 --> 00:55:10,825
So keep liking me.

758
00:55:11,725 --> 00:55:13,746
And pay for it.

759
00:55:32,547 --> 00:55:36,927
I'll remember.

760
00:55:42,339 --> 00:55:43,536
Stop!

761
00:55:43,536 --> 00:55:44,979
Hey!

762
00:55:51,136 --> 00:55:53,623
Cut! Hold on.

763
00:55:55,492 --> 00:55:56,870
Sir.

764
00:55:56,870 --> 00:56:00,979
Could we go handheld up to this alley?

765
00:56:00,979 --> 00:56:03,440
You're kidding, right?

766
00:56:03,440 --> 00:56:05,973
You want me running with the camera?

767
00:56:05,973 --> 00:56:08,532
No. The blocking's too tight.

768
00:56:08,532 --> 00:56:10,409
The crew will keep getting in frame.

769
00:56:10,409 --> 00:56:14,609
I want the audience
to feel chased with Moo Gyeom.

770
00:56:14,609 --> 00:56:20,316
The tension has to peak
for Crow's rescue to land.

771
00:56:20,316 --> 00:56:21,946
Let's try it once in rehearsal.

772
00:56:21,946 --> 00:56:25,334
If it doesn't work, I'll drop it.

773
00:56:28,000 --> 00:56:29,577
Fine.

774
00:56:29,577 --> 00:56:31,257
Thank you.

775
00:56:31,917 --> 00:56:33,553
Let's go handheld.

776
00:56:33,553 --> 00:56:36,533
Producer Nam! Where are you now?

777
00:56:36,533 --> 00:56:38,857
The actor is here...

778
00:56:45,744 --> 00:56:47,261
Yi Jae!

779
00:56:48,177 --> 00:56:50,644
Oh my gosh. You okay?

780
00:56:50,644 --> 00:56:52,798
Who did this?

781
00:57:07,341 --> 00:57:09,163
That was dangerous.

782
00:57:14,431 --> 00:57:15,841
Director Ju.

783
00:57:15,841 --> 00:57:17,668
Seong Moo?

784
00:58:06,421 --> 00:58:08,391
<i>How did you feel hearing about me?</i>

785
00:58:08,391 --> 00:58:09,989
<i>That's enough.</i>

786
00:58:09,989 --> 00:58:12,428
<i>You know what she and I are.</i>

787
00:58:12,428 --> 00:58:15,351
<i>That you were her first love?</i>

788
00:58:15,351 --> 00:58:16,495
<i>I love you.</i>

789
00:58:16,495 --> 00:58:18,108
<i>You don't remember that day?</i>

790
00:58:18,108 --> 00:58:19,261
<i>Stop drinking.</i>

791
00:58:19,261 --> 00:58:21,498
<i>I want to see what you'll do if I get drunk.</i>

792
00:58:21,498 --> 00:58:23,255
<i>It's just us here.</i>

793
00:58:23,255 --> 00:58:24,505
<i>So be honest.</i>

794
00:58:24,505 --> 00:58:26,106
<i>Remember this place?</i>

795
00:58:26,106 --> 00:58:29,925
<i>I liked you ten years ago, and I still do.</i>

796
00:58:29,925 --> 00:58:32,953
<i>You're still hung up on your first love?</i>
